<title>USA: Port of Portland, Ore., yields 5.97 pct in 2026.</title>
<headline>Port of Portland, Ore., yields 5.97 pct in 2026.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co said</p>
<p>Wednesday it tentatively priced $142.5 million Port of</p>
<p>Portland, Ore., airport bonds at a top yield of 5.97 percent</p>
<p>in 2026.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>THE PORT OF PORTLAND, OREGON</p>
<p>RE: $142,465,000*</p>
<p>PORTLAND INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT</p>
<p>REVENUE BONDS, SERIES ELEVEN</p>
<p>PRELIMINARY PRICING IS AS FOLLOWS:</p>
<p>SUBJECT TO ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>						AA-(UNDERLYING)</p>
<p>FGIC INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 09/15/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 01/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON	  PRICE</p>
